    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - GlobeeDorm\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nGlobee Dorm\nGlobee Dorm\nGlobee Dorm Rate\nSeoul Campus\nHUFS directly manages Globee Dorm and the International Houses. Payment for HUFS-managed dormitories is done in the first week of the semester by cash only.\nGlobeeDorm\nRegular Semester (16 weeks) 1,191,000 KRW\nVacation (8 weeks) 804,000 KRW (Students can apply for the Globee Dorm during the vacation period only if they lived at the Globee Dorm in the previous semester)\n*Additional fees: Deposit (30,000 KRW) and Student Council Fee (10,000 KRW)\n※ Dormitory Fee could be changed with prior notice.\nAddress\nSeoul Campus\nHUFS GlobeeDorm (Room # )\nHankuk University of Foreign Studies\n107 Imun-ro, Dongdaemun-gu, Seoul 02450, Korea\nGLOBEE DORM\nLocation\nCurfew System\nWeekday (Mon-Thurs.) Curfew: Midnight (12:00 am)\nOvernight stays (outside of the dorm)\nmust be reported to the dorm office\nin person before 10:00 pm.\nFailure to do so will result in 10 penalty points.\nYou can only stay out ONE TIME per week Monday through Thursday.\nYou must register this with GlobeeDorm through wis.hufs.ac.kr\nWeekend/Holiday Curfew (Friday, Saturday, Sunday): 12:00 am\nOvernight stays (outside of the dorm)\nmust be reported to the dorm office\nin person before 10:00 pm.\nFailure to do so will result in 10 penalty points.\nThere is NO limit for staying out overnight on the weekends or holidays.\nYou must register this with GlobeeDorm through wis.hufs.ac.kr\nPenalty Point System\nIf you receive more than 20 penalty points,\nyou will be expelled\nfrom the dorm.\nThings that are NOT permitted in the dorm\nUnreported overnight stays outside of the dorm\nActs of violence, theft, gambling\nExcessive noise and other disruptive behavior\nAbusive or harassing behaviors\nDrinking alcohol, partying\nWearing shoes in your room\nCooking\nYou cannot go to the opposite gender’s floors. Having members of the opposite gender in your room will result in\nimmediate expulsion\n.\nHow to Apply to Stay out\n1. Apply through wis.hufs.kr.\nHowever, the option to apply to stay out is ONLY available in Korean. It will NOT show up if you use the English language option.\n2. Days Available and Registration Button\nYou can see how many \"stay out\" days are left during the semester for weekdays with the first arrow on the left. The second arrow points to the button that you need to press to apply to stay out.\n3. Details of the \"Stay Out\"\nClick the calender icon to set the day you are staying outside of the dorm.\nEnter the reason you are staying out.\nProvide an emergency contact information such as your cell phone number.\n4\n. Details of the \"Stay Out\"\nAfter you save (successfully), you will see a log of your stay out. If you decide to change your plans and not stay out, you should delete this using the\n삭제\n(delete)\nbutton\nso it does not count against your week-day stay outs.\nRefund Policy\nThere are NO refundes for GlobeeDorm as your application is a 100% guarantee to get a room, which takes the room away from others who want to stay in GlobeeDorm. If you think you may not like GlobeeDorm, cancel you dorm room before checking in to the dorm and find other accomodations.\nApplication: Download\nSeoul Campus\nOffice of International Admissions & Management\nHankuk University of Foreign Studies\n107 Imun-ro, Dongdaemun-gu\nSeoul 02450, South Korea\nTel: +82-2-2173-2062\nFax: +82-2-2173-2877\nEmail:\nexchange@hufs.ac.kr\nHomepage:\nhttp://international.hufs.ac.kr\nStudent Guidebook:\nhttps://hellohufs.hufs.ac.kr\nFacebook:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hufsinternationalexchange/\nTwitter: @studyinkorea\nGlobal Campus\nOffice of International Admissions & Management\nHankuk University of Foreign Studies\n81 Oaedae-ro, Mohyun-eup, Cheoin-gu, Yongin-si\nGyeonggi-do 17035, South Korea\nTel: +82-31-330-4734\nFax: +82-31-330-4736\nEmail: hufsinbound@hufs.ac.kr\nHomepage:\nhttp://international.hufs.ac.kr\nStudent Guidebook:\nhttps://hellohufs.hufs.ac.kr\nFacebook:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hufsinternationalexchange/\nTwitter: @studyinkorea\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
